<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output up 6.6 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output up 6.6 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) rose 6.6 percent in March after a 2.7 percent fall in February, and was 4.8 percent higher than in March 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.  </p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	MARCH     FEBRUARY    MARCH 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	  6.6    -2.7 (-2.8)	10.6</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		  4.8     8.8 (-8.7)	 7.0</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)   128.0     N/A(120.5)	 N/A</p>
<p> mining m/m change		  -2.4   -11.0(-10.2)	 8.1</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change	     -12.4    -3.1 (-2.2)	 7.1</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	  8.4    -1.4 (-1.5)	10.9</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	9.0    11.7 (11.4)	 6.7</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		0.0    -6.0 (-5.8)	10.4</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	  -10.5    -1.2 (-1.0)	 9.5</p>
<p>NOTES - Revised data in brackets. March 1997 and February 1997 had 21 working days while March 1996 had 23 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
